.TH KAE-TOOLS 1 "November 2026" "KAE @KAE_VERSION@"
.SH NAME
kaegzip, kaezstd, kaelz4, kaeunzstd, kaezstdcat, kaezstdmt, kaezstdgrep, kaezstdless \- Kunpeng accelerated compression tools
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kaegzip
.RI [ gzip-options ] " [files]"
.br
.B kaezstd
.RI [ zstd-options ] " [files]"
.br
.B kaelz4
.RI [ lz4-options ] " [files]"
.SH DESCRIPTION
These commands invoke the KAE variants of gzip, Zstandard and LZ4.
Their options and data formats follow the corresponding upstream tools.
Use the command's --help option for the complete option list.
The kae-prefixed Zstandard helper commands provide the corresponding
unzstd, zstdcat, zstdmt, zstdgrep and zstdless operations.
.PP
Executables are stored in /usr/libexec/kae. The wrappers set PATH to use
the matching private helper programs. KAE compression libraries are
stored in the architecture-specific /usr/lib directory's kae subdirectory.
The system compression programs and libraries are not replaced.
.PP
Hardware acceleration requires supported Kunpeng accelerator devices and
the matching kae-driver package. Running without devices tests software
operation only.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
kaegzip -c input > input.gz
kaegzip -d -c input.gz > restored
kaezstd -c input > input.zst
kaelz4 -c input > input.lz4
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gzip (1),
.BR zstd (1),
.BR lz4 (1)
.PP
The upstream manuals are also supplied under
/usr/share/doc/kae-zip/upstream-man.
